  speakerName: RONNIE
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Now it''s your turn to introduce yourself.


    In Ilokano, ''ti
    nagan ko ket...'' means ''my name is...''


    The words ''ti nagan ko ket''
    form the fixed part of the phrase. You then complete the sentence by introducing
    yourself.


    For example, you can say ''ti nagan ko ket...'' followed by your
    own name.


    Now, introduce yourself using ''ti nagan ko ket...'' and say
    your own name.'
